.Dd July 25, 2026
.Dt JG-LIST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jg-list
.Nd recursively list files in a directory
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm jg
.Cm list
.Op Fl e Ar extensions
.Op Fl i Ar ignore-pattern
.Op Fl 0
.Op Ar paths
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.de QQ
.	ie t .Ql \\$*
.	el   .Dq \\$*
..
.Nm
recurses through one or more directories and lists \
their contents to standard output,
sorted alphabetically and depth-first.
Results are separated by either
.Tn ASCII Dv NUL No bytes
.Pq if the Fl 0 No switch is used
or newlines.
The command is analogous to the POSIX command
.Xr find 1 ,
except its output is ordered depth-first
.Pq directories listed before their contents ,
results are printed as resolved paths,
and symbolic links are never followed.
Moreover,
the subcommand works on Windows platforms,
and it offers a much more concise syntax,
albeit with far fewer bells and whistles.
.Pp
An alias of this command is supported when invoked via the
.Xr jg 1
wrapper
.Pq Ql Nm jg Cm ls ,
though its use is discouraged,
as it exists solely to alleviate the frustrations of users \
whose muscle-memory is conditioned to type
.QQ ls
instead of
.QQ list .
This is concession is handled solely by the
.Xr jg 1
front-end;
no accompanying
.Pa bin/ls.mjs
file exists,
not even as a symbolic link.
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl e , -extensions Ar list
Print only those results whose
.Xr basename 3
ends in one of the specified file extensions.
The
.Ar list
is separated by commas and/or whitespace,
and extensions may be specified with or without a leading dot.
This option may be used multiple times.
.
.It Fl i , -ignore Ar pattern
Filter out results whose paths match the given
.Ar pattern ,
which is a regular expression of the form
.Sm off
.Qq Sy "(?" Ar flags Sy \&) Ar source ,
.Sm on
used in JavaScript as
.Ql Ic new Cm RegExp Ns Pq Ar source , flags .
By default,
files named
.Li .git
or
.Li node_modules
are excluded from searches.
.Pp
This option may be used multiple times;
if so,
paths need only match one of the given
.Ar patterns
to be filtered from the output.
.
.It Fl m , -match Ar pattern
Filter results whose paths match the given
.Ar pattern .
Thi is the logical inverse of
.Fl -ignore ,
and may be used in conjunction with
.Fl -extensions .
Like
.Fl -ignore ,
the
.Fl -match
option may be used multiple times;
unlike its counterpart,
.Em all
patterns must match a path for it to survive filtration.
This is in addition to matching any file extensions specified by
.Fl e .
.
.It Fl 0
Separate results with
.Tn ASCII Dv NUL No bytes
instead of newlines,
suitable for consumption by
.Dq Nm xargs Fl 0 .
.
.It Ar paths
A list of directories to search.
If no
.Ar paths
are specified,
the current working directory is searched instead.
Note that symbolic links will
.Em not
be followed.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4n -compact
.It 0
Successful execution.
.It 1
No matching files were found.
.It 2
One or more of the search
.Ar paths
referenced a non-existent resource,
or one that isn't a directory.
.It 3
Some other,
unaccounted for exception occurred.
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh EXAMPLES
List image files in the directory
.Pa docs :
.Dl Nm jg Cm list \
 Fl e Ar jpeg,jpg \
 Fl e Ar png \
 Fl Ar e gif \
 Fl Ar e webp \
 Fl Ar e bmp \
 Ar ./docs
.Pp
List JavaScript files in current working directory,
excluding those in the
.Pa build
and
.Pa coverage
directories:
.Dl Nm jg Cm list \
 Fl e Ar js,mjs,cjs \
 Fl i No \(aq Ns Ar (?i)(?:^|/)(build|coverage)$ Ns No \(aq
.Pp
Report problematic filenames
.Pq those with contain embedded newlines :
.Dl Nm jg Cm list Fl 0m Qo Ar \en Qc | \
 Nm xargs Fl 0n Ns Ar 1 \
 Nm printf Qo File contains illegal character: %s\en Qc
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr jg 1 ,
.Xr ls 1 ,
.Xr xargs 1 ,
.Xr jg-list 3
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh HISTORY
The core logic of
.Nm
was originally written as part of
.Xr jg-lint 1 .
It was split into its own subcommand on January 24, 2019.
On December 22, 2019,
the command's
.Fn ls
function,
which handled the heavy lifting of recursive directory traversal,
was moved to the
.Lk "https://github.com/Alhadis/Utils" "utility library"
that
.Nm jg
already had a runtime dependency on.
.
